ks can be regarded as a set of six epistemological rules for falsifying propositions of the theory. In particular, the Purification postulate—the only one that is not shared with classical theory—allows falsification of random-sequences generators, a task classically unfeasible.</jats:p>\\\", \\\"URL\\\": \\\"https://doi.org/10.3390/e24040434\\\", \\\"published\\\": {\\\"date-parts\\\": [[2022, 3, 22]]}}, {\\\"DOI\\\": \\\"10.4324/9781003152156-39\\\", \\\"title\\\": [\\\"Arabic Epistemology of Reflection of Transcendence\\\"], \\\"URL\\\": \\\"https://doi.org/10.4324/9781003152156-39\\\", \\\"published\\\": {\\\"date-parts\\\": [[2021, 3, 24]]}}, {\\\"DOI\\\": \\\"10.1080/02691728.2025.2480274\\\", \\\"title\\\": [\\\"Talking to Myself: AI and Self-Knowledge\\\"], \\\"URL\\\": \\\"https://doi.org/10.1080/02691728.2025.2480274\\\", \\\"published\\\": {\\\"date-parts\\\": [[2025, 4, 3]]}}]\", \"excerpt_truncated\": false, \"source_sha256\": \"625f8e2a106fafcdb90141c86a0c6f7edb33fd4e72ab19337ef86424d4fcda6d\", \"verification_required\": true, \"topic_domain\": \"assumption_challenge\", \"evidence_role\": \"discovery\", \"host_tier\": \"discovery\", \"source_identity\": null, \"persistent_identifiers\": [\"doi:10.4324/9781003152156-20\", \"doi:10.3390/e24040434\", \"doi:10.4324/9781003152156-39\", \"doi:10.1080/02691728.2025.2480274\"], \"source_candidates\": [\"https://doi.org/10.4324/9781003152156-20\", \"https://doi.org/10.3390/e24040434\", \"https://doi.org/10.4324/9781003152156-39\", \"https://doi.org/10.1080/02691728.2025.2480274\"], \"source_candidate_identities\": {}}", "id": "source-f3cfe6e7064d442a", "scope": "collected", "source": "https://api.crossref.org/works?query=automated+falsification+and+self+reflection+in+AI+epistemology&rows=4&select=DOI%2Ctitle%2Cabstract%2CURL%2Cpublished"}, "prev_hash": "551dc259e02b9c36f0a8f67c518d7e474990c041ce66b66229569cbca1493f37", "hash": "0a257d22807309b6a8e45391137fc0fb8155d2d772a461c117bd14d630a7c09b"}, {"seq": 2311, "t